<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Tukaroi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1575">1575</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Mughalmari</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Tukaroi was fought on 3 March 1575 near the village of Tukaroi in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balasore">Balasore</a> district, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, between the Mughal army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a> under Munim Khan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/todar-mal">Todar Mal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daud-khan-karrani">Daud Khan Karrani</a>, sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>. Daud was defeated and signed the Treaty of Katak, giving up Bengal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a>, but he soon renewed the war and was finally defeated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajmahal">Rajmahal</a> in 1576.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tukaroi.jpg" alt="Battle of Tukaroi" width="320" height="288" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Manohar, 1590 artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Tukaroi_(3_March_1575).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
